{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner direction for N5 f1af7cfd / a18f373c after reading the complete installation note at exact 6e6447f5f83f59816adebd94c1eb3fa1e90418be, complete starter revision2 at 7736157b4c209aaada85059c91852c5f3a7908f5, the original N5 request and f12cef6b request, and targeted public protocol/types and source at d691e6e9 (main sources at e6e67828). These are proposed design defaults and corrections, not a guarded independent verdict, adoption, current deployed witness or implementation commission. Preserve all original N5/N3 conditions, C3/C4/C5/N1/N2/N6 ownership, full Stage4 and f12 job-authority scope. Keep formal invitations behind current verifier/full MCP review for now; no additional first-Jam gate, spike rerun or runtime suite for these prose edits.\n\nDECISIONS IN SECTION6.1\n1. Prefer retaining the existing platform warning behavior for this release and specifying an application compatibility rule in the guide: a routine update preserves a currently authorized, reachable release/exit act for every affected live holder, including supported recovery after an expired lease, until those holds are explicitly settled. The note's D1→D2 example keeps accept unchanged; add revision2's resume recovery explicitly and pin its exact input. Retire in two documents only after observed authoritative held-work state and deliberate holder transitions support it. This is application/update guidance, not a new Room admission rule or an assertion that an admin is physically unable to remove an exit. Do not add a refusal, automatic system release or silent rebinding as implementation in this request. Their contracts and runtime effects remain unadopted alternative work if an accepted use case calls for them.\n2. Identify the missing complete, consistent activation-impact inspection and dry run as N5-owned design dependencies coordinated with N1 where proposal reads are involved, rather than saying nobody owns them. Start by explaining what the existing authorized lanes/members/acts/log/proposal interfaces can show and what they cannot: a composed advisory inspection is not an atomic server preview. Scope/limit the retained cursor/head, completeness, pagination and race qualifications. Invitations are not in the public Roster type; no invented invitation-list API or credentials in a public report. Do not add contract/Room/client/CLI/MCP APIs merely to make this draft's table look runnable. A new authoritative read/preview contract is separately reviewed under the existing N5 design/later implementation process when the actual live-update task needs it; not a first-Jam prerequisite.\n3. The public validatePolicyV2 already accepts PolicyV2Context.historicalOpeningKinds and checkers (candidate packages/policy/src/acts.ts:163–186, exported by index.ts). The missing convenience is obtaining an authoritative complete history set, not adding the validator argument. Current lanes expose kind, and retained log opened effects expose opening kind/binding; bounded known history can supply advisory local context with a stated cursor/completeness limit. Absence from an incomplete local input is not proof the Room has no historical kind. Final proposal validation remains authoritative. Do not require a new read simply to pass an already supported parameter, and do not claim local validation matches the Room without complete appropriate context.\n4. Before the first outside checker binding, document the operator request and source/deployment review path using this project's existing gitseq tracking. Name the exact source revision and build/entrypoint, requested binding and Room/deployment, checker configuration/version and namespace, operator who deploys, and admin who enrolls/revokes the checker member and activates its configuration. Operator service binding alone supplies no Room membership or admin act. Keep the original f12cef6b contract decision, unsigned/forged/replayed-job threat model, effect on R-OBL/R-CARRY and A/G lane-edit list separate; it is not implementation or cross-account transport delivery. No actual binding, credential, deploy, human message or publication is performed by this direction.\n5. Retain no cross-account checker transport now, triggered by the first accepted task needing that actual boundary. Name planner as coordinator and builder as future design owner under the N5 gap, with original f12 authority design as a dependency. Do not silently enlarge f12's limited contract amendment into cross-account transport/runtime work. Retain both proposed HTTPS signed-job and pull shapes as alternatives, with authentication/replay/read-token/revocation/cleanup design then required. Review by an independent actor remains an honest initial route where the application asks for review; it never substitutes for an actual required machine check.\n\nSOURCE CORRECTIONS AND QUALIFICATIONS\nA. Lease retirement is not a guaranteed deadline while renewal continues. R-LANE-5 renews a current holder's lease; source admission.ts dispatches platform renew regardless of declared kind, threadCheck bypasses it, and renew performs authority/holder/lease/recovery/policy checks then renewLease. A still-authorized holder under policy that permits renew can continue it even after its opening/release kinds were removed. Thus 'lease bounds the harm' or 'ends when lease runs out' needs the condition that no accepted renewal extends it; do not promise a maximum wait from the current lease length. This is a source-qualified observation, not a runtime probe or a finding against the currently guarded candidate.\nB. A declared release name and unchanged binding alone do not prove a holder's usable exit. BindingSubject deliberately excludes who; current roles, delegability and delegation context, policy refusals, targeted thread kind, lease generation and required fields still matter. State those assumptions for the worked example and preserve the holder's actual qualifying exit in the general guidance. The structural hold-unending warning only checks for a release/hand-over declaration naming the opening kind (policy acts.ts soundness); it does not prove per-holder reachability or authorization.\nC. Narrow the initial-install grant sentence to grants made under v1 before the FIRST v2 activation. R-DECL-17 retains their platform-kind intersection and grants no declared kinds. A grant under an already-active v2 document retains each unchanged per-kind binding across an update; not every pre-update grant becomes empty. Keep the worked stale delegation/unredeemed invitation decisions qualified by the example's unchanged valid authority and source R-DECL-16/17 order.\nD. Re-signing after a definite unrecorded binding-stale refusal is distinct from retry after an uncertain answer. R-DECL-16 explicitly permits a caller to sign the same intended action under a new binding with the same idempotency key after that definite refusal; this is not a protocol defect. Never rebuild a pending/unknown act or reinterpret an admitted receipt. A changed intent is a deliberate new action; starter section7 chooses a fresh key for its new action as an application convention, not a universal prohibition of R-DECL-16. Show which path the guide uses and preserve original prepared intent/operation history. In section4.8 settle retained intent first as applicable, then decide new intent; do not say every pending act simply finishes under the new meaning.\nE. Complete Stage4 job support remains owed, but its kind/binding fields are not wholly missing from this candidate. jobs.ts signedAs, its ...signedAs spread at job assembly, reboundSince and binding-stale reissue path are present at d691e6e9. Qualify these as candidate source, not an observed end-to-end v2 job result or completed Stage4. Keep prepared/check-unroutable and the complete Stage4 producer/consumer/type/evidence requirements owned and open. Apply the same correction to starter section2.4; do not say no v2 job metadata exists or silently claim the complete route delivered.\nF. Distinguish supported source/configuration and dated live checker reports from a fresh deployed route witness. Checkers README describes three implementations and service bindings on main; this planning read does not prove the current production binding/configuration, any outsider's provisioning, or v2 functionality at the current deployment.\nG. Describe activation unambiguously: the policy-activated event names the new version; earlier admitted ordinary acts retain their original meaning and later acts use the newly active document. Reader catalogue intervals use since \u003c= seq \u003c until (policy catalogue.ts governs). Avoid saying the activation event itself is an ordinary act judged under the old document. Preserve recomputation/fencing/completion-forward qualifications, not an unqualified whole-system simultaneous transition claim.\nH. Log verification statements must name supported versions/mode, retained inputs and actual proof limits, consistent with adopted015/016 and the currently outstanding verifier review. Current source selecting D(s) is not independent approval or evidence that every fresh clone necessarily verifies every entry or proves full carry duty coverage/publication completion. Keep I5 as later deployed recorded acceptance, not a rerun now.\n\nSMALL STARTER FOLLOW-UPS AFTER COMPLETE7736157b READ\n1. Genesis requires a recovery key (R-GEN-1/3, RoomDraft). Setup currently lists only pat/ada/rev keys. Specify the distinct recovery key, storage and custody in the development setup, without enrolling it as a member or hiding an operator credential. A protected development file is an example, not production offline recovery delivery. Saved founding state must remain tied to those original keys.\n2. Give the exact signing call: signValue(\"artroom-genesis-v1\", genesis, signer) already canonicalizes/domain-tags its value internally (candidate keys.ts). Do not pass canonicalBytes(genesis) as the value or sign twice. This is a source contract clarification, not an executed founding result.\n3. A handed-over tarball run is a useful label IF it occurs, not a newly mandatory third acceptance run between builder evidence and qualifying cold acceptance. Remove that extra gate. The original cold run, supported-client coding/actual-Jam interaction, compact focused invariants and one justified external smoke remain required; combine witnesses where the same run genuinely proves them. No repeated whole-platform gate or runtime checks for documents alone.\n4. Source requests.ts confirms workspace opening is request-driven; describe the question's unused workspace as source-qualified, not measured zero provider cost. Explicitly reserve the desk/questions namespace or bound coding claims so the useful code change is not blocked by the question hold. Random scope names do not prove collisions impossible; conflict/refusal/reconciliation remains explicit, with durable per-question IDs on retry. No new collision test quota.\n5. For scenario2's permitted non-holder release, R-ADM-8 records steps7–9 refusals and returns their act ID. State that existing contract expectation instead of treating recordedness as an implementation choice. Keep the authorization/body assumptions, and show Pat as role admin (implicit permission) rather than two simultaneous technical roles.\n6. The per-run local-server authorization token has a different purpose from Room/bearer/session/workspace credentials. State how the page obtains and presents that local token, while Room credentials/signing keys stay in Node. Name the pinned CLI install/use needed by a separately controlled reviewer; do not hide that provisioning step. These resolve the proposed flow, not new production custody or transport work.\n\nUpdate both notes and their input pins/correction maps; do focused whitespace/source/pin checks only. Their complete independent design review/adoption and later normal exact-head implementation review remain owed. Original three browser/cloud/device stories and all their C1–C6 acceptance remain full scope, not supplied by this development starter.","body":{"head":"6e6447f5f83f59816adebd94c1eb3fa1e90418be","no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"Proposed installation/evolution guidance and source-qualified corrections; full N5/N3 scope and independent adoption remain owed.","source_approval":"none"}}